@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# CONTRACT — T7 Plugin Marketplace
+
+Conforms to `src/types.ts` interfaces (read-only). Modules share only types, never import each other.
+
+## 1. Registry (`src/registry/index.ts` → `createRegistry(): RegistryService`)
+- [ ] `register(manifest)` stores a manifest; multiple versions of same name coexist → test: register two versions, both retrievable
+- [ ] `register` upserts: re-registering same name+version replaces it → test: register twice, listVersions has 1 entry
+- [ ] `get(name)` returns highest semver version manifest or null → test: returns latest version; null when absent
+- [ ] `getVersion(name, version)` returns exact match or null → test: exact + null cases
+- [ ] `list()` returns all manifests across all versions → test: count matches
+- [ ] `search(query)` matches name/description/author case-insensitive substring → test: finds by partial name & description
+- [ ] `remove(name, version)` removes specific version, returns bool → test: true on hit, false on miss
+- [ ] `listVersions(name)` returns versions sorted descending (semver) → test: order correct
+- [ ] `update(name, version, updates)` merges partial updates → test: field updated, others intact
+
+## 2. Resolver (`src/resolver/index.ts` → `createResolver(): ResolverService`)
+- [ ] `satisfies(version, range)` delegates to semver → test: 1.2.3 satisfies ^1.0.0, not ^2.0.0
+- [ ] `maxSatisfying(versions, range)` returns highest satisfying or null → test: picks max; null when none
+- [ ] `validRange(range)` true/false → test: "^1.0.0" true, "garbage" false
+- [ ] `resolve(constraints, available)` returns ResolvedVersion[] for each satisfiable constraint → test: resolves multiple; skips unsatisfiable/missing
+
+## 3. Runner (`src/runner/index.ts` → `createRunner(): RunnerService`)
+- [ ] `execute(code, context)` runs code in vm, returns success result with output/duration/memoryUsed → test: `result = 1+1` returns output 2, success true
+- [ ] context variables passed into sandbox → test: context {x:5}, code `result = x*2` → 10
+- [ ] runtime error → success false, error message populated → test: `throw new Error('boom')`
+- [ ] `executeWithTimeout(code, ms, ctx)` kills runaway code, success false, timing recorded → test: `while(true){}` with 100ms → success false, error mentions timeout
+- [ ] `execute` uses a default timeout → test: default does not hang forever
+- [ ] duration >= 0 and memoryUsed is a number → test: assert types
+
+## 4. Reviews (`src/reviews/index.ts` → `createReviewSystem(): ReviewService`)
+- [ ] `addReview` assigns id, createdAt, flagged=false → test: returns populated review
+- [ ] `getReviews(pluginName)` returns reviews for plugin → test: filtered correctly
+- [ ] `getAverageRating(pluginName)` averages non-flagged; 0 when none → test: excludes flagged; 0 empty
+- [ ] `flagReview(id)` sets flagged true → test: flagged excluded from average
+- [ ] `getFlaggedReviews()` returns flagged only → test
+- [ ] `removeReview(id)` returns bool → test true/false
+- [ ] `getReviewsByUser(userId)` filter → test
+- [ ] `getReviewCount(pluginName)` count → test
+- [ ] Uses better-sqlite3 (in-memory) for persistence
+
+## 5. Deps (`src/deps/index.ts` → `createDepsService(): DepsService`)
+- [ ] `buildTree(name, registry)` builds DependencyNode tree from manifests → test: nested structure correct
+- [ ] `detectCycles` returns cycle paths or null → test: A→B→A returns cycle; acyclic returns null
+- [ ] `hasCircularDependency` boolean → test
+- [ ] `topologicalSort` returns deps-before-dependents order → test: order valid; throws/handles cycle
+- [ ] `flattenDependencies` returns unique transitive dep names → test: dedup + transitive
+- [ ] handles missing deps gracefully (not in registry) → test: no crash
+
+## 6. Integration (`src/index.ts` → `createMarketplace()`, `installPlugin(manifest)`)
+- [ ] exposes registry, resolver, runner, reviews, deps
+- [ ] `installPlugin` validates name/version/entryPoint → test: missing field throws/returns error
+- [ ] registers plugin → test: in registry after install
+- [ ] resolves dependency versions against registry availability → test: resolved array
+- [ ] rejects on circular dependency → test: cycle → rejected
+- [ ] executes entryPoint in sandbox → test: result returned
+- [ ] returns { resolved, execution } → test: shape correct
+
+## Validation (all must pass)
+- [ ] `npm run build` clean
+- [ ] `npm run lint` clean
+- [ ] `npm test` all pass
